"""IMU, motor current amplifiers, the four wall sensors with their shared emitter current sink, and
the two encoder slots.

IMU, IC2 (LSM6DSV, DS13476 Rev 5) on the shared SPI bus with its own chip select IMU_SPI_CSn;
INT1 (pin 4) on IMU_INT to PC7 (EXTI7), INT2 (pin 9) unconnected. The firmware routes every
interrupt it uses to INT1, the INT2 ones through CTRL4 (13h) INT2_on_INT1 (Table 58: the movable
INT2 interrupts are ORed onto INT1 and not fed to INT2), so one pin drives the line, push-pull and
active high at its defaults (IF_CFG PP_OD = 0, H_LACTIVE = 0, Tables 28-29), and needs no pull.
INT2 is an output forced to ground by default (Table 22, Internal pin status), so it is left open.
Mode 1: SDx and SCx grounded, OCS_Aux and SDO_Aux open (Table 2 p10). C24
and C25 100 nF on Vdd and Vdd_IO (Table 2 note 1, Figure 27 p44). On 3V3_D, as on the v1 main board
(the research keeps it there: +0.65 mA on 3V3_A if it moves).

Motor current, U10 (right motor) and U11 (left motor): INA241A2IDGKR, gain 20 V/V (TI SBOSA30D;
research Current sensing and A.3), across the 10 mOhm 4-terminal shunts R65 / R75 on the
drivers sheet, IN+ on the bridge-side sense terminal and IN- on the motor side, with no input
filter (the 25-45 uA input bias makes any series resistance an error, section 6.5). VS on 3V3_A
with C100 / C103 100 nF at the pin (section 8.3.1, the one bypass capacitor of Figure 8-3); REF1,
the pin beside VS, on the same 3V3_A node, so that capacitor holds it too, and REF2 on GND: the
bidirectional mid-supply output of section 7.4.3.2, VOUT = 20 x 10 mOhm x I + 3V3_A / 2,
ratiometric to VDDA, which 3V3_A also feeds. Range: (3.3 V - 0.2 V - 1.65 V) / 0.2 V/A = +7.25 A
and (1.65 V - 0.02 V) / 0.2 V/A = -8.15 A (output swing, section 6.5), above the 2.97 A ITRIP plus
its overshoot. The output drives the ADC through R78 / R79 150 Ohm (R_iso) with C102 / C105 1 nF
X7R after it, on the ADC line (Current_Sensor_Right on PC1, a slow ADC channel,
Current_Sensor_Left on PA6, a fast one; main.zen's pin budget). Section 6.5 rates 1 nF straight on
OUT ("no sustained oscillations", no isolation resistor); TI's INA241A2 PSpice model (SBOMC92)
gives 4.2 dB of peaking and 26 % overshoot there, and behind 150 Ohm a flat response at the pin
(-3 dB at 0.93 MHz, no overshoot;
research/next-revision/calculations/current_sense/ina241_riso.py, ina241_riso_out.txt). The
resistor also takes the ADC's sampling charge: the 4 pF sample capacitor (DS13311 Table 84)
arrives at another channel's voltage (the wall sensors and the battery share ADC1/ADC2) and kicks
C_f by up to 13 mV (66 mA), and since the INA241's output impedance rises to about 55 Ohm at 1 MHz
(Figure 6-24) the pin rings back instead of settling as R_iso x C_f. 150 Ohm damps that ring: the
error stays under 1 mA from 0.61 us on in every corner of the model (C_f +-25 %, X7R's +-10 % and
+-15 % over temperature, the ADC switch resistance, which DS13311 does not publish, 50-1000 Ohm,
2-10 pF on the pin, VCM 0-16.8 V, and the model's output impedance raised to Figure 6-24's),
against 0.84 us with the basic 100 Ohm part, which still leaves 1.40 mA at 0.8 us. The firmware
samples PA6/PC1 for at least 0.7 us (boards/main/firmware_changes.toml, current;
tests/test_main.py). C102 sits 3.5 mm from PC1; C105 sits beside R79, 23 mm of track from PA6,
since the escapes and lanes of the STM32's front-left pad row leave no spot by the pin (layout
README). An estimate, not a datasheet figure: the track's ~20 nH between C105 and the 4 pF
sample capacitor rings above 500 MHz,
damped by the ADC switch's resistance within nanoseconds, well inside the sampling time. On
the slow channel one conversion per PWM centre still fits (research H7 pin budget).

Wall sensors W1-W4: each an upright wall-sensor board (boards/wall: an SFH 4550 emitter over a
TPS601A phototransistor, the emitter resistor with its 1 uF, and the emitter's selector with its
AC-coupled gate network) standing on a wall joint (components/micras/WallJoint, spec/main.toml
[w1]-[w4]) whose 2x3 plated holes take the long pins of the 2x3 header straddling the wall board's
bottom edge: 1 OUT (Wall_Sensor_n), 2 GND, 3 3V3_A, 4 3V3_D, 5 SINK (EMITTER_SINK), 6 PWM
(Wall_Sensor_PWM_n, the selector's TIM3 channel).
The main board keeps the shared constant-current emitter sink, whose set-point the MCU's DAC
writes (research IR emitters and A.4; the model is
research/next-revision/calculations/emitter/emitter_sink.py, its results emitter_sink_out.txt),
and each receiver's load at its ADC:
- Sink: U12 (TLV9001IDBVR, SBOS833R) on 3V3_A with C106 100 nF; OUT through R82 100 Ohm to the
  gate of Q9 (AO3400A), whose drain is EMITTER_SINK and whose source is SINK_SENSE, the top of
  R83 1.2 Ohm 0.1 % (RT0603BRD071R2L, Kelvin-connected). 175 mA is 0.210 V across R83.
- Set-point: Wall_Emitter_Set (PA5, DAC1_OUT2, output buffer off) through R80 200 kOhm to
  SINK_SET (IN+), R81 20 kOhm to GND. With the buffer off the DAC swings 0 V to VREF+ through
  its 10.3-16 kOhm output resistance (DS13311 Table 90), so IN+ = VDAC x 20 / (RO + 220) kOhm,
  0.0858 at RO 13 kOhm, and the divider's 220 kOhm is a light load for that resistance; VREF+ is
  VDDA, 3V3_A, on this package (DS13311 Figures 46-47 note 1), so the emitter current is
  ratiometric to the ADC reference. At reset and with the DAC off, PA5 is a floating input
  (DS13311 Table 7 notes) and R81 holds IN+ at 0 V: the sink is off.
- Compensation: IN- (SINK_FB) is R93 1 kOhm from SINK_SENSE, with C113 1 nF X7R from OUT to IN-,
  so the loop is an integrator the TLV9001 drives into Q9's 630 pF Ciss (AO3400A p2; SBOS833R
  rates 500 pF), and over C113's X7R spread (+-10 %, +-15 % over temperature) it settles within
  1 % in 28.3 us at the latest with the same peaks (emitter_sink_out.txt section 3c); R94 200 kOhm
  from 3V3_A puts 3.3 V x 1 / 201 = 16.4 mV on IN-, beyond the +-2 mV input offset over
  temperature (SBOS833R 7.10), so a zero set-point drives Q9 off instead of leaving U12 at Q9's
  threshold. The current is I = (1.005 x IN+ - 16.4 mV) / 1.2 Ohm: code 3258 gives 175 mA at RO
  13 kOhm (172.7-177.3 mA over RO 10.3-16 kOhm), code 4095 223 mA, 58 uA per code
  (emitter_sink_out.txt section 4). Static errors, the DAC's +-12 LSB total unadjusted error and
  +-1 % gain error (buffer off, DS13311 Table 91), RO, R80/R81 1 %, the op-amp offset and R83 0.1
  %, are a gain each sensor's calibration takes in; 3V3_D and the emitter's VF do not enter. What
  a calibration cannot take in is RO's drift after it, which DS13311 does not give; but Table 90's
  10.3-16 kOhm bounds RO over every operating condition, so the drift of one part stays inside
  172.7-177.3 mA, +-1.3 % about the typical 13 kOhm (2.6 % if a part swung end to end), against
  the emitter's own -0.5 %/K (SFH 4550 v1.9 p5, TCI).
- Emitter n: the wall board's R1, 3.3 Ohm 0603, from 3V3_D to the LED anode (the joint's
  emitter_resistor); the LED cathode on the drain of the wall board's selector Q1 (AO3400A),
  whose source is the joint's SINK pin, EMITTER_SINK. At VF max (1.79 V at
  175 mA between the SFH 4550's maximum points, p5) and 3V3_D at 3.229 V (its 3.284 V minimum
  less the 22 mV emitter droop and a 33 mV ESP32 dip, research power-tree study section 6), the
  selector and Q9 keep 3.229 - 1.79 - 0.175 x 3.3 - 0.21 = 0.65 V. The firmware lights each
  emitter 150 us per 1 ms frame, 15 % (MicrasFirmware config/targets/v1/target.hpp), so the
  3.3 Ohm carries 101 mW during a pulse and 15 mW on average (25 mW at the 223 mA full scale):
  UNI-ROYAL rates the 0603 1/10 W continuous to 70 C, derated linearly to 0 at 155 C (82 mW at
  85 C), and 2.5 x its rated voltage, 6.25 x the power, for 5 s (thick film chip resistor data
  sheet V.3, 2019, sections 6, 9 and 11), so a 150 us pulse of 101-164 mW is far inside it. Q9
  carries the sink's 175 mA 60 % of the time at VDS = 3V3_D - VF - I x 3.3 Ohm - 0.21 V, at most
  0.98 V (3.346 V, VF 1.575 V on the p5 chord) and 1.15 V for a VF as low as 1.4 V: 0.17-0.20 W in
  a pulse, 0.12 W on average, 15 K above ambient at the AO3400A's 125 C/W maximum steady-state
  RthJA (p1; PD 1.4 W at 25 C).
  The resistor also limits the emitter current when the sink fails on (Q9 shorted or U12 stuck
  high): (3.346 V - VF) / (3.3 + 1.2 Ohm) is about 0.35 A with VF on the chord of the p5 typical
  points, inside the SFH 4550's 0.38 A pulse rating at tp 150 us and D 0.2 (25 C chart,
  WallSensor.zen), so a failed sink does not overstress the emitters while the AC-coupled
  selectors still pulse them. The sink's own full scale (code 4095 at VDDA 3.36 V and RO
  10.3 kOhm) is 0.23 A. A 2.2 Ohm basic part would give the selector 0.19 V more headroom but let
  a failed sink drive 0.44 A, above the rating; 4.7 Ohm leaves the selector 0.41 V
  (boards/main/test/test_sensors.zen, emitter_pulse_within_rating). The pulse rating falls with
  temperature: the 85 C chart allows about 0.07 A at D 0.2, and by the chart's scaling (an
  inference, WallSensor.zen) 223 mA at full scale holds to about 56 C ambient, 175 mA to about
  65 C.
- Selector gates: on the wall board, AC-coupled as on the v1 main board (R 220 Ohm from PWM, C
  220 nF to the gate, R 22 kOhm and a 1N4148WS clamp to GND), so a PWM pin held high cannot keep
  an emitter on; the analysis and the numbers are in boards/wall/wall.zen and its bench.
- Firmware: one emitter at a time; two selectors on together share the set current. The DAC
  holds the sensor's code only while that sensor's selector is on: it steps up at or after the
  selector's rising edge and back to 0 at or before its falling edge, and stays 0 in the dark
  slot. Then, in TI's TLV9002 PSpice model (the TLV9001's dual) with Q9 fitted to the AO3400A's
  datasheet, from a minimum-threshold part to a maximum one at -40 C and with +-2 mV of offset,
  the pulse rises without overshoot to within 1 % 7.4-13 us after the selector's edge, over 60 us
  before the scan starts at 75 us; a gate of twice the datasheet's capacitance (the level-3
  AO3400 stand-in, -40 to 85 C) overshoots to at most 233 mA and is within 1 % after 18 us. A DAC
  that leads or trails its selector by 5 us lets U12 saturate: the pulse starts at up to 275 mA
  and is within 1 % after 28 us, still before the scan. Every peak stays under the SFH 4550's
  0.38 A pulse rating (emitter_sink_out.txt section 3). The codes set each emitter's brightness
  (boards/main/firmware_changes.toml, emitters).
- Receiver n: the phototransistor collector on 3V3_A (joint pin 3), its emitter on the joint's OUT,
  Wall_Sensor_n (ADC), with R14/R18/R22/R26 1 kOhm to GND on the main board, between the joint and
  the ADC pin (R18 9 mm, R14 13 mm, R26 13 mm and R22 29 mm of track from the pin): the
  phototransistor is a current source, so the signal crosses the joint as a current. The follower stops at 3V3_A - VCE(sat) (0.4 V max, TPS601A(F)
  p2), below VREF+ = 3V3_A, so neither the lit nor the dark reading leaves the ADC's range: ambient
  light only takes up the receiver's headroom, which the firmware watches (a dark reading above
  80 % of full scale is a blind sensor, MicrasFirmware wall_sensors_config). The datasheet rates
  IL at 0.1 mW/cm2 of 2870 K tungsten light, about 17 lux of it: 100 uA min, up to 1.2 mA in rank
  C (p2). Through the receiver's 10 degree lobe (p4) a white wall lit by 500 lux of halogen light
  (the All Japan contest's heats, 400-500 lux; NTF 2005) gives 0.37 mA typical, 11 % of full scale,
  and 1.7 mA for a rank C part; 1500 lux, its spot-lit final, 1.4 mA typical (41 %), and a rank C
  part saturates; 1500 lux of LED or fluorescent light 0.11-0.49 mA; a window or a lamp in the
  line of sight saturates any part (research/next-revision/calculations/emitter/ambient_light.py).
- 3V3_A during a pulse: the emitters are on 3V3_D, so only a receiver's current (2.9 mA at most,
  the follower's ceiling) and U12's gate drive step on 3V3_A. ADP7142 Rev K Figure 38 (VOUT 3.3 V,
  COUT 2.2 uF) reads 44 mV for a 1-200 mA step, so under 5 mA VDDA moves by at most 1.1 mV, 0.03 %
  of the ADC reference (C81 leaves 4.4 uF effective, which halves it again). ngspice has no ADP7142
  model to run: the bound is the datasheet's.
- The wall board's C1, 1 uF on 3V3_D next to its emitter resistor.

Encoder slots EC1 (right wheel) and EC2 (left wheel), as on the v1 main board: the AS5047U encoder
boards on the SPI bus, each with its own CSn, plus the ABI A/B outputs to timer inputs; 1 uF +
100 nF at each slot (C69/C70 at EC1, C71/C72 at EC2) on 3V3_D.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Spi")
load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "C_1N_0402",
    "C_1U_0402",
    "R_100_0402",
    "R_150_0402",
    "R_1K_0402",
    "R_1R2_0603_0P1",
    "R_200K_0402",
    "R_20K_0402",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
AO3400A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/aos/AO3400A/AO3400A.zen")
EncoderSlot = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/micras/EncoderSlot/EncoderSlot.zen")
INA241A2 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/INA241A2/INA241A2.zen")
LSM6DSV = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/LSM6DSV/LSM6DSV.zen")
TLV9001 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/TLV9001/TLV9001.zen")
WallJoint = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/micras/WallJoint/WallJoint.zen")

# Its own sheet in the board schematic (layout/main.kicad_sch).
Project(name="Sensors", path="layout", layout=False)

# A signal port takes the name of the board net it carries (the firmware's pin label) wherever
# that name is an identifier, so its sheet pin and hierarchical label match the root's label:
# KiCad's ERC flags labels whose names differ only in case (similar_labels).
V3V3_D = io(Power)
V3V3_A = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)

# The SPI bus enters once, with each device's chip select: SCK, MISO and MOSI are shared, and
# three Spi ports would repeat them as nine sheet pins.
SPI_SCK = io(Net)
SPI_MISO = io(Net)
SPI_MOSI = io(Net)
IMU_SPI_CSn = io(Net)
Encoder_Right_CSn = io(Net)
Encoder_Left_CSn = io(Net)

IMU_INT = io(Net)

MOTOR_L_SENSE_P = io(Net)
MOTOR_L_SENSE_N = io(Net)
MOTOR_R_SENSE_P = io(Net)
MOTOR_R_SENSE_N = io(Net)
Current_Sensor_Left = io(Net)
Current_Sensor_Right = io(Net)

Wall_Sensor_PWM_0 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_PWM_1 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_PWM_2 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_PWM_3 = io(Net)
Wall_Emitter_Set = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_0 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_1 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_2 = io(Net)
Wall_Sensor_3 = io(Net)

Encoder_Right_ABI_A = io(Net)
Encoder_Right_ABI_B = io(Net)
Encoder_Left_ABI_A = io(Net)
Encoder_Left_ABI_B = io(Net)

IMU_SPI = Spi(CS=IMU_SPI_CSn, CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)
ENCODER_RIGHT_SPI = Spi(CS=Encoder_Right_CSn, CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)
ENCODER_LEFT_SPI = Spi(CS=Encoder_Left_CSn, CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)

SINK_SET = Net("SINK_SET")
SINK_SENSE = Net("SINK_SENSE")
SINK_FB = Net("SINK_FB")
SINK_GATE = Net("SINK_GATE")
SINK_OUT = Net("SINK_OUT")
EMITTER_SINK = Net("EMITTER_SINK")

# IMU.
LSM6DSV(
    name="IC2",
    VDD=V3V3_D,
    VDDIO=V3V3_D,
    GND=GND,
    SPI=IMU_SPI,
    INT1=IMU_INT,
    INT2=NotConnected(),
    SDX=GND,
    SCX=GND,
)
Capacitor(name="C24", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C25", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)


# Motor current amplifiers.
def current_amplifier(side, amp, c_vs, r_iso, c_f, sense_p, sense_n, adc):
    out = Net("CURRENT_{}_AMP".format(side))
    INA241A2(
        name=amp,
        VS=V3V3_A,
        GND=GND,
        IN_P=sense_p,
        IN_N=sense_n,
        REF1=V3V3_A,
        REF2=GND,
        OUT=out,
    )
    Capacitor(name=c_vs, P1=GND, P2=V3V3_A, **C_100N_0402)
    Resistor(name=r_iso, P1=out, P2=adc, **R_150_0402)
    Capacitor(name=c_f, P1=GND, P2=adc, **C_1N_0402)


current_amplifier("R", "U10", "C100", "R78", "C102", MOTOR_R_SENSE_P, MOTOR_R_SENSE_N, Current_Sensor_Right)
current_amplifier("L", "U11", "C103", "R79", "C105", MOTOR_L_SENSE_P, MOTOR_L_SENSE_N, Current_Sensor_Left)

# Emitter current sink.
TLV9001(name="U12", VCC=V3V3_A, GND=GND, IN_P=SINK_SET, IN_N=SINK_FB, OUT=SINK_OUT)
Capacitor(name="C106", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_A, **C_100N_0402)
Resistor(name="R80", P1=Wall_Emitter_Set, P2=SINK_SET, **R_200K_0402)
Resistor(name="R81", P1=GND, P2=SINK_SET, **R_20K_0402)
Resistor(name="R93", P1=SINK_SENSE, P2=SINK_FB, **R_1K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C113", P1=SINK_OUT, P2=SINK_FB, **C_1N_0402)
Resistor(name="R94", P1=V3V3_A, P2=SINK_FB, **R_200K_0402)
Resistor(name="R82", P1=SINK_OUT, P2=SINK_GATE, **R_100_0402)
AO3400A(name="Q9", G=SINK_GATE, S=SINK_SENSE, D=EMITTER_SINK)
Resistor(name="R83", P1=SINK_SENSE, P2=GND, **R_1R2_0603_0P1)


# Wall sensors.
def wall_sensor(sensor, r_load, pwm, out):
    WallJoint(name=sensor, PWM=pwm, SINK=EMITTER_SINK, V3V3_D=V3V3_D, GND=GND, OUT=out, V3V3_A=V3V3_A)
    Resistor(name=r_load, P1=GND, P2=out, **R_1K_0402)


wall_sensor("W1", "R14", Wall_Sensor_PWM_0, Wall_Sensor_0)
wall_sensor("W2", "R18", Wall_Sensor_PWM_1, Wall_Sensor_1)
wall_sensor("W3", "R22", Wall_Sensor_PWM_2, Wall_Sensor_2)
wall_sensor("W4", "R26", Wall_Sensor_PWM_3, Wall_Sensor_3)

# Encoder slots.
EncoderSlot(name="EC1", VDD=V3V3_D, GND=GND, SPI=ENCODER_RIGHT_SPI, A=Encoder_Right_ABI_A, B=Encoder_Right_ABI_B)
Capacitor(name="C69", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_1U_0402)
Capacitor(name="C70", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
EncoderSlot(name="EC2", VDD=V3V3_D, GND=GND, SPI=ENCODER_LEFT_SPI, A=Encoder_Left_ABI_A, B=Encoder_Left_ABI_B)
Capacitor(name="C71", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_1U_0402)
Capacitor(name="C72", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
